  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "xmlParseNCNameComplex",
    "file": "libxml2/parser.c",
    "description": "Global-buffer-overflow is caused by xmlParseNCNameComplex computing a name length (`len`) by repeatedly calling CUR_CHAR/NEXTL without ensuring enough buffered input/termination, then passing `(BASE_PTR + startPosition, len)` to xmlDictLookup. xmlDictLookup/xmlDictAddString trust `len` and memcpy that many bytes, so an over-read occurs from parser input/global tables (seen as read past `xmlIsPubidChar_tab`). Crash manifests in xmlDictAddString memcpy, but the root cause is unsafe length derivation in xmlParseNCNameComplex.",
    "conditions": "In the xslt harness, attacker-controlled stylesheet data triggers xsl:import loading and XML parsing of imported content. A malformed/non-UTF sequence in a start-tag/QName path forces xmlParseQName -> xmlParseNCName -> xmlParseNCNameComplex. The parser derives an excessive `len` for the NCName and interns it via xmlDictLookup, which copies `len` bytes from an invalid source span, producing ASan global-buffer-overflow during memcpy."
  },
